    [CI] Add unregistered GLM-5.2 A3 static and super kernel case (#17685)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Add a standalone optional GLM-5.2 W8A8C8 A3 128K internal-DP
    configuration based on #17871. Both deployment commands enable
    `enable_npugraph_ex`, `enable_static_kernel` and `enable_super_kernel`,
    with shared `LOCAL_WORLD_SIZE=16` for four local DP replicas and TP4.
    
    The new file uses the distinct test name
    `multi-node-GLM-5.2-W8A8C8-MTP-A3_128k-static-super-kernels`. Model,
    two-node topology, MTP settings, benchmark workloads, baselines and
    thresholds follow #17871.
    
    **The case is intentionally unregistered in both nightly and weekly
    matrices.** `weekly_config.yaml` and all existing registered
    configurations remain unchanged; periodic scheduling and slash-command
    selection will not dispatch this optional case. Registration requires a
    separate change after runtime validation. This PR contains only the
    optional YAML file. The five GLM nightly configurations and their
    runtime support are tracked separately in #18246.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. This preserves an optional CI configuration for review. Prior #17871
    runs encountered device timeouts/traps; this PR does not claim to fix
    the underlying issue or demonstrate a passing benchmark.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Parsed YAML and all JSON-valued options in both deployment commands;
    checked `LOCAL_WORLD_SIZE` and all three compilation flags.
    - Checked that the new test name and file are absent from every periodic
    matrix.
    - `git diff --check`: passed.
    - `bash format.sh ci`: attempted using an LF copy because the Windows
    checkout uses CRLF; blocked by missing `pre-commit` in Bash, not
    reported as passed.
    - NPU end-to-end execution: pending. No nightly or weekly command was
    posted.
    
